This method is intended to return true if n (n ≥ 2) is prime. For which input does it give the wrong answer?

```java
public static boolean isPrime(int n) {
    for (int d = 2; d < n / 2; d++) {
        if (n % d == 0) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

