```java
public static int digitalRoot(int n) {
    while (n >= 10) {
        int sum = 0;
        while (n > 0) {
            sum += n % 10;
            n /= 10;
        }
        n = sum;
    }
    return n;
}

public static int longestRun(String str) {
    int best = 1;
    int current = 1;
    for (int i = 1; i < str.length(); i++) {
        if (str.substring(i, i + 1).equals(str.substring(i - 1, i))) {
            current++;
            if (current > best) {
                best = current;
            }
        } else {
            current = 1;
        }
    }
    return best;
}
```

In (a), the inner loop sums the digits and the outer loop repeats until one digit remains. In (b), updating best inside the matching branch ensures a run that ends at the last character is still counted.
